# Mobile full player fixed-region contract

The full player is a fixed-height region above scrollable panes. The region keeps its geometry while
chips and pane content below it change.

## Required

- Only the viewer band flexes. Every other band keeps its fixed height. The viewer band flexes for
  real (`flexGrow` / `flexShrink` with `minHeight: 0`) and sizes its square from its own measured
  box, so a band whose text grows with the OS font setting takes that space from the artwork
  instead of pushing the transport rows out of the region.
- The artwork is what gives way. It has caps (`FULL_PLAYER_ARTWORK_MAX_PHONE` /
  `_MAX_TABLET`) but no floor: a viewport too short for the fixed bands shrinks the square rather
  than pushing the chip strip off the bottom edge. The region is never taller than the space the
  viewport can give it, and clips (`overflow: 'hidden'`) in the worst case.
- Region sizing comes from `fullPlayerLayout.ts`; do not introduce ad-hoc magic heights in screen
  styles. Band styles read the same constants the math reads (`FULL_PLAYER_REGION_GAP`,
  `FULL_PLAYER_CONTROL_STACK_GAP`, `FULL_PLAYER_REGION_TOP_PADDING`,
  `FULL_PLAYER_REGION_BOTTOM_PADDING`, `FULL_PLAYER_CHIP_HEADER_HEIGHT`) so reserved and rendered
  space cannot drift.
- Episode title and channel title share one title block (`FULL_PLAYER_TITLE_BLOCK_HEIGHT`) with a
  tight internal gap. Do not split them into two bands separated by `FULL_PLAYER_REGION_GAP`.
- Band order matches web's player modal: title block, artwork, segment band, progress, transport,
  utility. Upper seams use `FULL_PLAYER_REGION_GAP` (three of them). Progress → transport and
  transport → utility use the tighter `FULL_PLAYER_CONTROL_STACK_GAP` (two of them). Plus
  `FULL_PLAYER_REGION_TOP_PADDING` above the title and `FULL_PLAYER_REGION_BOTTOM_PADDING` below the
  utility row (the seam before the section chips). Both paddings are chrome so the bands sum to the
  region height rather than overflowing. The chip header has no hairlines.
- Peek reserves the chip strip plus the bottom safe-area inset, and a bottom fill covers the inset
  so pane copy cannot show there. The header does not include that inset, so chips stay close to
  pane content after scroll. `FULL_PLAYER_CHIP_HEADER_HEIGHT` is the default-text-size floor —
  the strip reports its measured height (`chipStripHeight`) and peek follows the larger of the two,
  so accessibility text sizes cannot leak Summary copy under the chips. Measure the chip row slot,
  never the header, or the condensed bar would change the reserve mid-scroll.
- The segment band (`FULL_PLAYER_SEGMENT_BAND_HEIGHT`) sits **below** the artwork and is reserved
  unconditionally, exactly as web reserves `--media-modal-subtitle-reserve`. A chapter or clip name
  arriving mid-playback fades into a row that is already there — it never resizes the artwork or
  moves the transport.
- Duration for the scrubber is seeded from `item.item_about.duration` via
  `resolveMediaFileDurationHintSeconds` when playback starts; native `durationSeconds > 0` still
  wins. The left clock always shows the playhead; seek stays disabled only while duration is still
  `0`.
- New player controls open sheets. Do not expand controls inline inside the fixed region.
- If a new control needs persistent space, reserve a fixed-height band for it in layout math.
- Sticky chips and the condensed bar belong to the scroll shell, not inside pane content.
- Video renders inside the measured artwork square and letterboxes when aspect ratios differ.
- Playhead UI lives in leaf components that read `playbackProgressStore`; the fixed-region shell
  uses `usePlaybackSession()` only.
- Pull-to-dismiss is the native-stack top-edge gesture only (`fullScreenGestureEnabled: false`).
- The pane `SectionList` does not bounce or over-scroll — this screen has no pull-to-refresh.

## Do not

- Do not conditionally insert or remove fixed-region rows. Content that comes and goes gets a
  permanently reserved band; anything else jumps the layout while a listener is watching it.
- Do not let pane loading, empty states, or chip switching push transport or utility rows.
- Do not bind region size to transcript/chapter/clip body height.
- Do not give the region a minimum height that can exceed the viewport, and do not reserve peek from
  a hardcoded chip height alone — both push the chip strip off-screen on short viewports or at large
  text sizes.
- Do not subscribe the shell to progress ticks (`usePlayback()` / `usePlaybackProgress()`).
- Do not enable a full-screen vertical dismiss gesture or list bounce on the full player.
